# Contact form — EmailJS
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the three values. Vite only reads
# them at startup, so restart `npm run dev` after creating it. Without them the
# form builds to `sendForm(undefined, undefined, form, undefined)` and every
# submission fails in the browser with no clue as to why.
#
# Where each one comes from, in the EmailJS dashboard:
#   Email Services  -> the service's Service ID
#   Email Templates -> the template's Template ID
#   Account         -> General -> Public Key
#
# Everything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the JavaScript the browser
# downloads, so only ever put the PUBLIC key here. EmailJS's private key is a
# server credential and would be readable by anyone viewing the bundle.
#
# The destination address lives in the EmailJS template, not here — which is
# why no email address ships with the site.

VITE_EMAIL_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_PORTFOLIO_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_API_KEY=
